+# 🚀 Putting Clipper AI on the internet
+
+You asked for **Vercel** — quick honest answer first:
+
+## Why Vercel can't run Clipper AI
+
+Vercel hosts small, short-lived website functions. Clipper AI is a **video
+rendering studio**: it runs FFmpeg for 15–60+ seconds per clip, transcribes
+audio for ~2 minutes, and stores uploaded videos on disk. That needs a real,
+always-on server — Vercel has no FFmpeg, kills anything that runs longer than
+a few seconds, and has no disk for your videos.
+
+What Vercel *is* great for: static blogs and Next.js sites. Not this.
+
+## The right host: Render (or Railway / Fly.io)
+
+These run full **Docker containers** — exactly what Clipper AI ships with now.
+Everything in this repo is already deploy-ready:
+
+| File | What it does |
+|---|---|
+| `Dockerfile` | Builds the app + FFmpeg + speech engine into one image |
+| `render.yaml` | One-click blueprint for Render.com (with a persistent disk) |
+| `DATA_ROOT=/data` | Uploads, renders and the database survive restarts |
+
+## Deploy in 4 steps
+
+**Step 0 — get this code onto GitHub.**
+This workspace can't reach GitHub (the session's GitHub link is closed), so
+start a **new Arena session** on this repo and ask: *"commit and push
+everything to GitHub"*. That gets every fix (Pro Polish quality pass, auto
+analysis, Clipper AI rename) into your repo.
+
+**Step 1 — create a Render account** at [render.com](https://render.com)
+(free signup, GitHub login).
+
+**Step 2 — deploy the blueprint.**
+Dashboard → **New → Blueprint** → pick your `website` repo → Render reads
+`render.yaml` and configures everything (Docker, health check, 10 GB disk).
+
+**Step 3 — wait ~5 minutes** for the image build. You'll get a live URL like
+`https://clipper-ai.onrender.com` — share it anywhere.
+
+## Cost (important)
+
+Video rendering is real computing, so free tiers don't cut it:
+
+- **Render Starter — $7/month** (recommended): 2 GB RAM, no sleeping,
+  persistent disk. Renders finish in 15–60 s.
+- Free alternatives (Render free / Hugging Face Spaces): too little RAM for
+  1080p renders and they sleep + lose uploads — fine for a demo, frustrating
+  for real use.
+
+## What works the same online
+
+Everything: upload → auto-analysis (pocketsphinx, offline) → suggested clips →
+17 styles incl. **Pro Polish** (−14 LUFS mastered audio, ducked music) →
+renders you can download. No API keys, no external services — the server does
+it all itself.
